1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,830
Volts, amps and ohms.

2
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:05,918
Picture electricity as water in a pipe.

3
00:00:06,098 --> 00:00:08,983
Volts are the push, like head: pressure
from height.

4
00:00:09,163 --> 00:00:13,494
Amps are the flow: how much charge passes
each second, like litres per second.

5
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:17,129
Ohms are resistance, like a narrow pipe
holding the flow back.

6
00:00:17,849 --> 00:00:21,838
Ohm's law ties them together: volts equal
amps, times ohms.

7
00:00:22,018 --> 00:00:25,507
Put 12 volts across 6 ohms, and 2 amps
flow.

8
00:00:25,687 --> 00:00:29,376
More push, more flow. More resistance,
less flow.

9
00:00:29,556 --> 00:00:35,778
And power, from episode two, is volts
times amps: 12 times 2 is 24 watts.

10
00:00:37,098 --> 00:00:40,635
Now send our stream's 245 watts down a
cable.

11
00:00:40,815 --> 00:00:43,799
At 12 volts, that's about 20 amps.

12
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:48,299
At 48 volts, about 5. A quarter of the
current.

13
00:00:48,479 --> 00:00:52,673
And the heat a cable wastes goes with the
current squared. A quarter of the current:

14
00:00:52,673 --> 00:00:53,871
a sixteenth of the heat.

15
00:00:54,051 --> 00:00:59,165
The same cable that wastes 42 W at 12
volts, a sixth of our power,

16
00:00:59,165 --> 00:01:00,792
wastes under 3 at 48.

17
00:01:02,712 --> 00:01:05,135
But low voltage is not the same as safe.

18
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:10,092
Short a battery, and it can push a huge
current: enough to make a spanner red hot,

19
00:01:10,092 --> 00:01:11,082
and start a fire.

20
00:01:11,262 --> 00:01:16,399
Take off rings and watches, use insulated
tools, and fit a fuse at the battery.

21
00:01:16,579 --> 00:01:19,974
And as always, a hydro generator never
runs without a load.

22
00:01:19,974 --> 00:01:22,679
Shut the water off before you touch the
wiring,

23
00:01:22,679 --> 00:01:25,097
and have a qualified electrician check it.

24
00:01:26,817 --> 00:01:30,104
Remember: volts, times amps, gives watts.

25
00:01:30,284 --> 00:01:33,198
For the same watts, higher volts means
fewer amps,

26
00:01:33,198 --> 00:01:35,180
and less heat lost in your cables.

27
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,659
Next: why your pipe eats your head.
